 ## [Unreleased]
 
+## [0.8.2] - 2026-11-19
+
+### Security
+- Fixed an arbitrary file write (GHSA-m9mq-7m7q-xc6p). `browser_download`'s `save_dir` is now confined under the download root (`~/.browse-mcp/downloads`, or `$BROWSE_MCP_HOME/downloads`), and the explicit `path` for `browser_save_state` / `browser_load_state` is confined under `~/.browse-mcp/state`. Absolute paths, `..` escapes, and symlink escapes are rejected. Download filenames are cut down to a bare basename.
+- The `force_fetch` fallback in `browser_download` now applies the `BROWSE_MCP_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` / `BROWSE_MCP_BLOCKED_ORIGINS` origin fence on every redirect hop. Before this fix a raw `fetch()` skipped the fence.
+
+### Changed
+- `save_dir` and the state `path` must now be relative to their data root. Callers that passed absolute paths must switch to relative sub-paths or move the data root with `BROWSE_MCP_HOME`.
+
 ## [0.8.1] - 2026-06-12
 
 ### Added
